From 3d99cc66ce06dbcc20e13499370346d4390619b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 03:53:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kanban: capsule-bound workers get a truthful /workspace
 contract and cwd [daveey]

A capsule-bound Kanban worker (tools.capsule_workspace bound by observation_bind) only has the task's
private git checkout mounted at /workspace in a runsc sandbox, and the host publishes its committed head.
Run6 (Ask Eve) showed every model-facing surface said otherwise: KANBAN_GUIDANCE told it to cd
$HERMES_KANBAN_WORKSPACE (unset in the sandbox) and to kanban_complete when a review child exists, the
first turn's Workspace header named the HOST worktree, and terminal commands ran in the profile's
terminal.cwd (/root). The worker probed host paths and blocked asking for a host backend and push
credentials.

- terminal/file default cwd: _get_env_config returns /workspace for a bound docker worker; the per-command
  resolver keeps only recorded cwds inside /workspace (an explicit workdir is still honoured).
- prompt: bound workers get kanban_capsule_guidance(): the generic protocol with its host-workspace,
  credential-example and step-5 completion lines replaced (exact anchors; drift fails that worker closed)
  plus a static Capsule contract (/workspace, safe.directory, no fetch/push/credential asks,
  kanban_request_review hand-off, host seals/tests/publishes/completes).
- worker context and kanban_show: the own card's Workspace header names /workspace; kanban_show adds
  execution_workspace. Task body text and the row's workspace_path are reported unchanged.

Ordinary (unbound) workers: byte-identical prompt and unchanged cwd (control tests).
